WEBVTT

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.820
Hey, come here. Help me take care of this.

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:42.584
What is this? You didn't chop it up?

00:00:43.627 --> 00:00:45.253
What am I supposed to do with it?

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:48.381
Well, I got into some shit. Help a brother out.

00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:50.217
Nobody told me.

00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:52.885
You're from Yes Money?

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.012
Course I am. We've met a few times already.

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:57.056
Moonsu and the other guys aren't with you?

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.850
Moonsu?

00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:02.312
Moonsu's probably at work right now. Duh.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.402
Just do me this favor.

00:01:19.121 --> 00:01:21.456
Who the fuck brings uncut meat?

00:01:28.839 --> 00:01:30.257
I appreciate this!

00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:26.354
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

00:02:26.355 --> 00:02:27.356
Heeju.

00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:30.734
I'm hungry.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.656
Oh, I'm so fucking starving right now!

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:09.272
Ah.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:15.862
Heeju.

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:19.282
You know, my dad...

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.744
...he was the same kind of asshole as your uncle.

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:26.164
He brought our whole family down with his gambling addiction.

00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:29.126
That piece of shit should have just died alone.

00:03:29.751 --> 00:03:31.420
He even tried to kill my mom and I.

00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:34.464
Anyway...

00:03:40.011 --> 00:03:41.221
Don't give it another though.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.432
I took care of the body.

00:03:44.683 --> 00:03:46.725
There's not a single shred of flesh left.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:47.978
Don't worry about it.

00:03:54.151 --> 00:03:56.403
This one? This one's mine?

00:04:03.618 --> 00:04:05.245
I said don't worry!

00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:09.123
Just let it go.

00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:15.422
I mean, that was a man who deserved to die.

00:04:18.175 --> 00:04:20.135
A man who deserved to die?

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:21.928
Mm-hmm.

00:04:25.474 --> 00:04:26.475
Hey.

00:04:28.143 --> 00:04:30.020
You see how important money is now? :cue

00:04:32.189 --> 00:04:33.732
It makes the world go 'round.

00:04:35.484 --> 00:04:38.819
Like, having money lets you do anything you could ever want.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.740
And it also lets you not do things you don't want.

00:04:43.617 --> 00:04:44.701
Oh, yeah.

00:04:45.702 --> 00:04:48.454
Here you go. As promised.

00:04:48.455 --> 00:04:49.538
Your new ID card.

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:51.373
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD JU HARAN

00:04:51.374 --> 00:04:52.458
I just went through all our debtors,

00:04:52.459 --> 00:04:54.293
and then I picked out who looked like you the most.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:57.046
We can take care of the passport and fingerprints and all that later.

00:04:57.047 --> 00:05:00.675
But for starters, open a bank account under her name.

00:05:01.927 --> 00:05:05.055
Well, obviously we're about to have piles of cash rollin' in.

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:07.974
So, can't exactly keep it all piled up in here.

00:05:08.266 --> 00:05:09.350
Hmm?

00:05:09.351 --> 00:05:11.061
Who is this lady?

00:05:11.645 --> 00:05:12.813
Ah, this lady...

00:05:14.815 --> 00:05:15.816
...she's dead.

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:18.401
It was suicide.

00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:20.070
A year ago.

00:05:21.863 --> 00:05:22.989
So they say.

00:05:25.408 --> 00:05:27.701
She doesn't exist in the world anymore.

00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:30.538
No one is looking for her, and there's no way to find her.

00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:32.290
And someone that young...

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.502
...you really think she had any money? They took her organs.

00:05:36.503 --> 00:05:39.297
She just doesn't exist. She's gone.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:46.137
I'll also turn out like that, if I get caught by your company people.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.850
So be good.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.561
Or else.

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:59.942
Anyway, we need to wrap this whole thing up quickly.

00:05:59.943 --> 00:06:03.320
Since Detective Kim is even involved now,

00:06:03.321 --> 00:06:04.446
it's a huge deal.

00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:07.074
I bet the guys at Yes Money are desperate to find you.

00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:08.076
What do we do?

00:06:08.869 --> 00:06:10.995
We got eight potatoes left, right?

00:06:10.996 --> 00:06:13.123
Let's craft and sell two at a time now.

00:06:13.999 --> 00:06:17.835
After selling so many one-kilo bars, I realized how fucking easy it is.

00:06:17.836 --> 00:06:19.253
If I just run my ass off,

00:06:19.254 --> 00:06:20.880
hitting all the jewelry shops,

00:06:20.881 --> 00:06:22.257
I can sell 20 in three days.

00:06:22.591 --> 00:06:23.842
It could be done in two weeks.

00:06:24.426 --> 00:06:25.509
In the meantime,

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.386
you should get your passport ready to go.

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:29.598
Then we'll go overseas. Simple.

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.060
What is it?

00:06:36.438 --> 00:06:38.565
You still don't trust me after all this?

00:06:39.524 --> 00:06:40.525
Heeju.

00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:43.486
We're way past being just business partners now.

00:06:44.863 --> 00:06:46.948
I even killed a man because of you.

00:06:48.658 --> 00:06:50.659
We're like bound by fate now.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.370
Bound by fate.

00:06:54.748 --> 00:06:56.207
I better get going.

00:06:57.959 --> 00:06:59.835
How many potatoes are you bringing next round?

00:06:59.836 --> 00:07:01.128
Two.

00:07:01.129 --> 00:07:03.297
Correct. Where do they need to go?

00:07:03.298 --> 00:07:05.049
To the shop.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.760
Correct. Where do you get those?

00:07:08.845 --> 00:07:10.095
I guess not. Okay.

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.597
You're too smart!

00:07:11.598 --> 00:07:13.016
I'm out.

00:07:14.225 --> 00:07:16.226
Ah, fuck, I'm so tired.

00:08:16.079 --> 00:08:19.748
EPISODE 5 SECRET

00:08:19.749 --> 00:08:21.625
JANGGAK TRADE INC.

00:08:21.626 --> 00:08:23.502
Can I help you?

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:26.797
Uh, hi. I want to buy a car today.

00:08:26.798 --> 00:08:27.881
You're here to get a car?

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:29.466
-  Yes. - Ah.

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:31.218
How did you hear about us?

00:08:31.219 --> 00:08:33.096
I run a pawnshop.

00:08:33.763 --> 00:08:34.888
You run a pawnshop?

00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:37.100
All right.

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:40.227
Let me show you our cars.

00:08:40.228 --> 00:08:42.855
- Okay. - Any particular type car you had in mind?

00:08:42.856 --> 00:08:44.356
Uh, no, not really.

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:46.025
No, okay then.

00:08:46.026 --> 00:08:47.109
Well, if that's the case,

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:49.903
then this one here is probably what you're looking for.

00:08:49.904 --> 00:08:51.780
It has good mileage, plus it's practically brand new.

00:08:51.781 --> 00:08:53.073
Huh.

00:08:55.285 --> 00:08:59.288
Now all you gotta do is take this to the district office

00:08:59.289 --> 00:09:00.789
and transfer the title.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.083
- Okay. - Here. :cue

00:09:03.001 --> 00:09:05.753
- You can take the car today. - Thanks.

00:09:05.754 --> 00:09:09.757
Actually, I was curious about your pawnshop.

00:09:11.051 --> 00:09:14.012
Is it here around the Jeongsan area?

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.389
Why do you ask?

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:20.393
It's just that there's not a pawnshop I don't know around here.

00:09:21.978 --> 00:09:24.813
It was originally run by a relative, and something came up,

00:09:24.814 --> 00:09:26.607
so I ended up taking it over.

00:09:26.608 --> 00:09:27.941
Ah.

00:09:27.942 --> 00:09:31.153
I was wondering, where do all the cars end up going?

00:09:31.154 --> 00:09:33.448
Most of 'em? Eh...

00:09:34.866 --> 00:09:36.325
Most of 'em end up overseas.

00:09:36.326 --> 00:09:38.827
What about the other collateral, besides the cars?

00:09:38.828 --> 00:09:41.956
Those other items normally end up overseas, too.

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:43.499
More or less.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:47.128
You only ship items overseas and don't ship anything back in?

00:09:50.131 --> 00:09:52.801
For a young lady, you sure are curious about all this.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.593
- Uh... -  I mean,

00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:56.053
you're askin' a lot of questions.

00:09:56.054 --> 00:09:58.555
Are you a cop or someone from customs?

00:09:58.556 --> 00:10:01.058
No, it's nothing like that. I'm just really curious.

00:10:01.059 --> 00:10:02.142
Actually, up until recently,

00:10:02.143 --> 00:10:05.104
I used to be in a similar line of work as you.

00:10:05.105 --> 00:10:07.440
Checking imported goods, clearing them for entry.

00:10:10.193 --> 00:10:12.152
Oh, really?

00:10:12.153 --> 00:10:14.948
Uh, one more thing.

00:10:16.199 --> 00:10:19.035
We've had this for a while, just hanging around the pawnshop.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:25.625
And I was wondering if you had any bullets for it.

00:10:26.668 --> 00:10:30.296
It's just sometimes working late nights alone can be kinda scary.

00:10:31.464 --> 00:10:32.589
Hopefully I never have to use it,

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:35.760
but just having it would make me feel so much safer.

00:10:36.678 --> 00:10:38.930
Yeah. Is that so?

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:40.557
You're a surprising young lady.

00:10:41.599 --> 00:10:43.225
I can give you however much you want.

00:10:43.226 --> 00:10:45.060
It's not about the money.

00:10:45.061 --> 00:10:46.938
Smuggling is just not what I do.

00:10:48.773 --> 00:10:50.649
Is it that you can't, or that you won't?

00:10:51.734 --> 00:10:53.485
Listen, I'm guessing since you're new in town,

00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:55.195
you haven't heard of me before.

00:10:55.196 --> 00:10:56.864
Do I look like someone who can't to you?

00:10:56.865 --> 00:10:58.407
Maybe I just don't wanna.

00:10:58.408 --> 00:11:01.326
I was thinking if you could get this for me,

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:03.620
then there could be other things you could help me with.

00:11:04.956 --> 00:11:06.958
However, if it's something that you don't do, then...

00:11:08.877 --> 00:11:11.837
What other sort of things did you need help with?

00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:14.590
Well, I don't know.

00:11:14.591 --> 00:11:16.926
There's nothing that a pawnshop doesn't have.

00:11:19.804 --> 00:11:20.805
Detonics.

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:24.184
Wait here a second while I go get them for you.

00:11:40.074 --> 00:11:42.075
So, have you fired a gun?

00:11:42.076 --> 00:11:43.536
Uh, no.

00:11:44.537 --> 00:11:47.247
It's not like I'd actually have a reason to use it.

00:11:47.248 --> 00:11:48.333
Uh-huh.

00:11:48.917 --> 00:11:50.959
First insert the magazine.

00:11:52.212 --> 00:11:54.254
Like that. After that,

00:11:54.255 --> 00:11:57.257
you grab this part and slide it back.

00:11:57.258 --> 00:11:58.800
When you do that,

00:11:58.801 --> 00:12:00.886
a bullet will be chambered here.

00:12:00.887 --> 00:12:02.512
And since it's very dangerous,

00:12:02.513 --> 00:12:04.848
you need to always keep the safety up,

00:12:04.849 --> 00:12:06.935
like so, until you need to fire.

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:08.894
It's the same with the trigger.

00:12:08.895 --> 00:12:11.981
Until you're ready, your finger stays back here.

00:12:12.899 --> 00:12:14.024
And when you shoot,

00:12:14.025 --> 00:12:17.028
always hold it with both hands.

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:18.612
Just like so.

00:12:18.613 --> 00:12:20.949
Most women find the recoil pretty strong.

00:12:21.908 --> 00:12:24.118
You see this? This waving?

00:12:24.869 --> 00:12:27.372
Any sort of movement affects your accuracy.

00:12:28.456 --> 00:12:29.623
The head and heart.

00:12:29.624 --> 00:12:32.251
That's where you aim, and if you don't hit them there,

00:12:32.252 --> 00:12:34.544
you keep shooting until they're dead.

00:12:34.545 --> 00:12:36.171
Bang!

00:12:36.172 --> 00:12:38.049
Bang, bang. Bang, bang.

00:12:38.841 --> 00:12:41.010
You want to kill, you keep shooting.

00:12:42.053 --> 00:12:43.054
Here.

00:12:45.765 --> 00:12:47.140
How much money do I owe you?

00:12:47.141 --> 00:12:48.433
Ah, no, no, no, no.

00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:50.603
I don't need money. It's a gift from me to you.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:57.568
In return, how about from now on, you only work with me?

00:13:21.801 --> 00:13:22.969
NAME JU HARAN :cue

00:14:12.518 --> 00:14:15.480
There's no one in this world who deserves to die.

00:14:16.898 --> 00:14:18.649
I killed so I can live.

00:14:19.525 --> 00:14:20.609
That's all it is.

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:24.238
Because I can't be the one to die.

00:15:04.362 --> 00:15:08.366
GANGWON SAEBAEK HOSPITAL

00:15:20.378 --> 00:15:22.171
Auntie.

00:15:24.006 --> 00:15:25.133
How are you doing?

00:15:30.012 --> 00:15:32.013
Yes?

00:15:34.684 --> 00:15:36.144
Why are you still here?

00:15:36.686 --> 00:15:38.062
You should lie down.

00:15:39.272 --> 00:15:40.398
The cash I gave you.

00:15:41.274 --> 00:15:42.358
Did you return it?

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:45.402
Is that...

00:15:45.403 --> 00:15:46.904
...why he dropped the charges?

00:15:48.447 --> 00:15:49.656
Mm-hmm.

00:15:49.657 --> 00:15:50.741
You crazy bitch.

00:15:51.659 --> 00:15:53.451
Why didn't you run when I told you to?

00:15:54.453 --> 00:15:55.954
You need to run away.

00:15:55.955 --> 00:15:57.664
Go quickly, before he comes back.

00:15:57.665 --> 00:15:58.666
It's all right.

00:15:59.375 --> 00:16:01.460
That man won't ever come back again.

00:16:02.044 --> 00:16:03.629
I'm telling you, he will!

00:16:04.839 --> 00:16:06.674
And then the both of us will be trapped here.

00:16:07.717 --> 00:16:10.845
He's already bleeding me dry. That's more than enough.

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:13.346
You-you have to go now.

00:16:13.347 --> 00:16:14.807
I don't have to.

00:16:16.267 --> 00:16:18.977
It's not like I have much time left. I don't need you. Just hurry up and go.

00:16:18.978 --> 00:16:21.105
Aunty, that's why I'm not leaving you.

00:16:22.523 --> 00:16:25.609
What'll it take, then? Should I hang myself?

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:27.736
-  Listen to me! - No!

00:16:32.116 --> 00:16:33.367
He has to be coming.

00:16:35.995 --> 00:16:37.246
He's coming, I said!

00:16:37.914 --> 00:16:39.539
You-you need to hide somewhere.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:41.458
- Look at me. Stop. -  Quickly.

00:16:41.459 --> 00:16:44.337
- You have to hide- -  Auntie. Auntie. Auntie.

00:16:45.463 --> 00:16:49.008
That asshole is never coming back.

00:16:49.967 --> 00:16:51.802
He can't come back.

00:16:56.515 --> 00:16:58.226
This time I made sure of that so now...

00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:01.938
...everything's gonna be okay.

00:17:08.694 --> 00:17:10.988
From now on, I'll stay by your side.

00:17:11.572 --> 00:17:14.575
:cue

00:17:23.209 --> 00:17:25.210
My chairman's losing patience now.

00:17:25.211 --> 00:17:27.171
All these construction delays.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:45.438
There are formal legal protocols to follow.

00:17:45.439 --> 00:17:49.234
Once your chairman signs off, we're ready to move immediately.

00:17:49.235 --> 00:17:51.027
Well, for that to happen,

00:17:51.028 --> 00:17:53.029
we're going to need a solid guarantee from you guys.

00:17:56.909 --> 00:18:01.746
Let's just say we'll need a reason to move.

00:18:13.634 --> 00:18:15.135
What did he just say?

00:18:21.309 --> 00:18:25.312
He wishes to speak with your chairman directly.

00:18:25.313 --> 00:18:26.939
No, what'd he say before that?

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:52.631
The chairman says,

00:18:52.632 --> 00:18:55.550
"The coffin in Korea's now your responsibility.

00:18:55.551 --> 00:18:58.511
So you will have to move it yourself."

00:19:38.219 --> 00:19:40.888
Something like this isn't complete without a drink.

00:19:42.932 --> 00:19:43.933
My chairman told me...

00:19:45.184 --> 00:19:47.061
...to take extra special care of you.

00:19:48.562 --> 00:19:50.606
He's committing everything to this deal.

00:20:14.964 --> 00:20:15.965
How's it goin'?

00:20:17.216 --> 00:20:18.466
Dokyung hasn't opened his mouth yet?

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:22.971
I'm sorry.

00:20:22.972 --> 00:20:24.223
Hocheol, come on.

00:20:28.102 --> 00:20:29.520
Didn't you tell me not to worry?

00:20:30.271 --> 00:20:33.398
You said that bastard has nowhere to run and that he's in your hands.

00:20:33.399 --> 00:20:34.900
So what now?

00:20:35.526 --> 00:20:39.362
I'll go to the hospital myself, then I'll shut him up.

00:20:39.363 --> 00:20:42.157
How, exactly? You said the cops are involved.

00:20:42.158 --> 00:20:45.536
I know a detective at the Gangwon Central Police Department.

00:20:46.746 --> 00:20:50.790
I might need to buy a little time to have a moment alone with Dokyung.

00:20:50.791 --> 00:20:52.250
And what if he still doesn't talk?

00:20:52.251 --> 00:20:53.461
Kill him?

00:20:54.336 --> 00:20:55.795
How would we find the casket?

00:20:55.796 --> 00:20:57.005
Worst-case scenario.

00:20:57.006 --> 00:21:00.885
Even if we have to give up the casket, shutting him up is the priority.

00:21:03.345 --> 00:21:04.972
Ah.

00:21:06.724 --> 00:21:08.224
Is that right?

00:21:08.225 --> 00:21:10.018
That's the priority?

00:21:10.019 --> 00:21:12.021
I didn't realize that.

00:21:14.732 --> 00:21:15.815
Hey, Hocheol.

00:21:15.816 --> 00:21:17.610
:cue

00:21:18.819 --> 00:21:20.570
Are you the boss now?

00:21:20.571 --> 00:21:22.740
Do you get to decide what's important?

00:21:25.034 --> 00:21:26.535
I'm sorry.

00:21:27.369 --> 00:21:29.412
I spoke out of turn.

00:21:29.413 --> 00:21:32.082
This bastard Lee Dokyung, he married?

00:21:32.625 --> 00:21:34.959
As far as I know, he's not married.

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:36.211
Hocheol, listen.

00:21:36.212 --> 00:21:38.296
Cut off a finger from a friend or a bitch close to him

00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:39.631
and send it to him.

00:21:39.632 --> 00:21:40.799
You think he won't talk after that?

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.927
Yes, I'll get on that right away.

00:21:43.844 --> 00:21:46.514
When you find the casket, don't open it right away.

00:21:47.807 --> 00:21:49.641
Give me a call first.

00:21:49.642 --> 00:21:51.268
I want to go check it myself.

00:21:52.478 --> 00:21:53.479
Yes, sir.

00:21:55.940 --> 00:21:58.107
Hocheol, make sure you get this right.

00:21:59.318 --> 00:22:01.528
That casket better be sitting in

00:22:01.529 --> 00:22:03.905
the hotel before I get back from this trip.

00:22:03.906 --> 00:22:04.907
Understand?

